All 9 agents patched. Now update the actual `.env` files — the key one for the Policyholder agents is `PolicyholderAgents/.env`:

```bash
BASE=~/Musaddique/AgentVerse_Claims_motor/Jarvis_claims_agents_v3_copy_new

# Update the two .env files the Policyholder agents read
sed -i 's|PHOENIX_ENDPOINT=.*|PHOENIX_ENDPOINT=https://app.phoenix.arize.com/s/musalalkot123|' \
  "$BASE/PolicyholderAgents/.env" \
  "$BASE/.env"

# Verify
grep PHOENIX_ENDPOINT "$BASE/PolicyholderAgents/.env" "$BASE/.env"
```

Also check that your API key is set in `PolicyholderAgents/.env` (should be your `ak-...` key):

```bash
grep PHOENIX_API_KEY ~/Musaddique/AgentVerse_Claims_motor/Jarvis_claims_agents_v3_copy_new/PolicyholderAgents/.env
```

If `PHOENIX_API_KEY` is missing or blank, add it:

```bash
echo 'PHOENIX_API_KEY=ak-YOUR-KEY-HERE' >> ~/Musaddique/AgentVerse_Claims_motor/Jarvis_claims_agents_v3_copy_new/PolicyholderAgents/.env
```

Then restart the agents. The first request after restart should log `Phoenix tracing enabled → https://app.phoenix.arize.com/s/musalalkot123` and spans should appear in your Phoenix Cloud dashboard under the `policyholder-agents` project.
